1238","description":"the nose and its diseases","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7d95-917e-8df451ef99f4","description":"ants","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7e7c-83cf-fe605adb0439","description":"origin of life","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7478-bc74-4b5cbd86b05f","description":"the age of trees and the records in their rings","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7d66-a7ae-5bfa934e2494","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What are the 2 parts of complex numbers known as?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"In a + bi, a is the real part, while b is the coefficient of the imaginary unit i.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554d-723d-bcb9-3cd7105cc953","description":"Real & Imaginary","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7331-81c4-5ffc1b012cc0","description":"True & False","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7cad-9ee0-6842073f77a7","description":"Big & Small","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7b1c-8da0-49e22121583c","description":"Logical & Intuitive","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7fca-9794-a97377347939","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which Soviet spacecraft carried the dog Laika into orbit in 1957?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Laika became the first animal to orbit Earth aboard Sputnik 2, but she did not return alive.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7e49-88b7-516343e87137","description":"Sputnik 2","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-70e7-8a66-9aebfba9e5b4","description":"Sputnik 1","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-785b-9e1f-17745774ddfd","description":"Vostok 1","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-72f9-8fba-ba6cd68c87aa","description":"Luna 2","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7f75-895a-acf9038d3455","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the smallest bird in the world?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Bee Hummingbird is native to Cuba, and females are slightly larger than males.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7d7a-a409-d8e0ba9ee6b9","description":"Bee Hummingbird","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7101-9e6a-2513aa738b7a","description":"Pigeon","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7291-9c30-0681c565968f","description":"Great Horned Owl","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7c51-8993-92e1663e7a2d","description":"Ostrich","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7534-b50e-60b39a8e9333","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What infectious lung disease is known by two letters?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"TB stands for tuberculosis, a bacterial infection that most often affects the lungs and can spread through the air.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554d-714d-a72c-8533b4a34e23","description":"TB","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-768c-aeac-e908d811bf43","description":"HF","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7c84-815b-22de7e336d6a","description":"CC","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7458-91a3-f259ad159a20","description":"AK","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-78ae-ae23-4bec8b3d101f","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Venereology the study of?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Venereology is the study of sexually transmitted diseases. Its name is related to \u201cvenereal,\u201d a term historically associated with Venus, the Roman goddess of love.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554d-74e3-97ee-2b8f1b90d50c","description":"Sexually transmitted diseases","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7b94-9415-0e2745656cf8","description":"Vocal sounds","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7e03-910e-4c9c24e1b276","description":"Grasshoppers and crickets","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-76c7-b3e0-8b274394f136","description":"Ants","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-741f-9d03-025a5305e815","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What upward force acts on an object that is immersed in fluid?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The buoyant force follows Archimedes\' principle: its magnitude equals the weight of the fluid displaced by the immersed object.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7f71-812e-e9c74f071b4b","description":"Buoyant force","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7aa3-8c7b-d321fd8ed413","description":"Shear force","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7293-b659-da2cea0ad8cb","description":"Viscous force","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-77fd-bdc1-18bf652f40b5","description":"Drag force","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7622-90f6-db3d36f46089","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"In laboratory settings, what word is used to refer to the act of stirring or shaking a liquid?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Agitating a liquid helps distribute its contents or resuspend settled material; a vortex mixer does this rapidly.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7a19-bb48-a5fe66d666b9","description":"Agitate","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7d12-995d-9341eaa1f32a","description":"Oscillate","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7e39-912d-6f0796e3401c","description":"Dilute","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7093-a5b8-571d85b57fbe","description":"Tremble","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-713b-8055-8535c01d166a","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"In 1898, which noble gas was discovered and named after the Greek word for \'hidden\'?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Krypton makes up only a tiny fraction of Earth\'s atmosphere, so it had to be isolated from liquefied air.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7dca-b987-6f66040605d4","description":"Krypton","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7b97-ad27-f28238443ff4","description":"Argon","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7e8d-b1cb-632ee4da8e45","description":"Helium","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7e69-b203-c68c43843e47","description":"Xenon","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7709-b1ec-cea4390ab99c","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the chemical mercury often used for?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Mercury is liquid at room temperature and expands predictably as it warms, making it useful in measuring instruments. Its toxicity has led to safer replacements in many applications.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554d-724e-8a56-401e64c9a305","description":"It is used in thermometers, thermostats, barometers","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7ea2-9ced-096f9c03eb61","description":"It is used as an ingredient in baking.","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7da9-9f7d-ad9beff4a749","description":"It is used as an ingredient in the production of glass, bricks, and ceramics.","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7b95-9e5c-9b18279b335c","description":"It is used in disinfectants and antiseptics.","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-778a-bc42-d671e0c104b8","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the word for a group of owls?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"A parliament of owls is the established collective noun. The same word names a legislative assembly, giving the phrase a stately tone.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554d-752f-99c4-f65c1ba95661","description":"A parliament","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-71b5-b336-673f30ce2da3","description":"A host","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7291-a9f5-4b87dfd0100c","description":"A nest","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-76fe-b323-6ce5356f33c2","description":"A yoke","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7153-b6eb-a074a89ac6ae","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b