wer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7a89-b296-073a79008cfd","description":"fermentation","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7fba-b36d-4806f0311d30","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Who invented dynamite?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Alfred Nobel patented dynamite in 1867, and his will provided for the prizes that bear his name.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7068-84f3-9d71f3ea9b85","description":"Alfred Nobel","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7797-894e-6ecb20e9bdca","description":"Nikola Tesla","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-771a-bfcc-251e8838da0a","description":"Thomas Edison","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-746a-918d-f01d3cd863f9","description":"Leonardo da Vinci","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7a59-9766-664ad5249192","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the SI unit of pressure?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The pascal is named after Blaise Pascal, a French mathematician and physicist who studied pressure.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554d-787e-abf4-63007341435d","description":"Pascal","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7919-941a-f1357afdba95","description":"Newton","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7c0a-9b48-39fba0eca034","description":"Joule","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7c7b-bba9-1cd8d85788b9","description":"Watt","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7364-96aa-f313458917f3","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the largest species of penguin?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The emperor penguin is the largest living penguin and breeds during the Antarctic winter.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7abe-bc73-d84dbe52b9be","description":"Emperor","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7fbb-b03f-0a9c82a53fcc","description":"King","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-773d-abc7-f0651166ae9a","description":"Gentoo","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-75ad-8e9c-02ce8e831fe2","description":"Ad\u00e9lie","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7b6f-afc4-2c1607f649f0","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the word for a young mule?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"A foal is the young of a horse or donkey. A mule is the hybrid offspring of a male donkey and a female horse.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7e36-8b85-a8bbb8f5f635","description":"A Foal","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-715b-89af-3e6439eb8c60","description":"A Cria","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7aae-9b81-0c6476b40dd6","description":"A Bunny","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7733-a221-8eb7f8bd6624","description":"A Lamb","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-79d8-b5f9-69619847d458","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What name is often used to refer to a type of flying possum?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"A glider has a membrane of skin between its limbs that lets it travel between trees without powered flight.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554d-769d-b5c5-717f25035d05","description":"A glider","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7cff-9685-9581337c0bdc","description":"A leaper","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7691-9cfe-e8f8d47fc8b6","description":"A flyer","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-79be-9c0b-a0c0f15cab77","description":"A hanger","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7925-9367-10c54a080f21","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is dry ice made of?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Carbon dioxide is called dry ice because it changes directly from a solid to a gas at ordinary pressure, without melting into a liquid.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554d-7133-8e67-d518b7618176","description":"Carbon dioxide","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb