ight angles, each measuring 90\u00b0, so their sum is 360\u00b0.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7430-89d2-61b8c3b25d95","description":"360\u00b0","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-799d-8c38-8eefaf99e81d","description":"480\u00b0","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7cdd-b4ec-5a785ccf44c9","description":"90\u00b0","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7b11-b55a-16beb0f1816f","description":"180\u00b0","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-716a-bd4a-ee1a72b8f248","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What was Colossus, the machine used at Bletchley Park during World War II?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Colossus was a code-breaking computer that analyzed Lorenz-encrypted German teleprinter messages using thousands of vacuum tubes.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7ba9-8ff8-23cbf4ec5d42","description":"A code-breaking computer","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7d26-a0a9-60613a7cad90","description":"A nuclear-resistant tank","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-73b7-b06b-b882cdfdb462","description":"A supersonic bomber","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7a97-84ca-b00d7f2cdd76","description":"An intercontinental missile","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-781c-a065-af2ace2e622c","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Ecophysiology the study of?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Ecophysiology links physiology with ecology, examining how conditions such as drought affect a plant\u2019s water use and growth.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7905-b308-761e3b69bba2","description":"How the environment interacts with an organism","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7ee3-854d-923a020a86f1","description":"The art of bell ringing","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7f06-a862-89fb42ed5509","description":"Bats","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7607-9db8-2327dcbf9e5c","descript