atives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554e-750e-bc83-55cbdb8549d9","description":"A gaggle","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7438-8180-e0146c69a1dd","description":"A nest","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7e0d-9476-918863693f62","description":"A pride","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7318-9cf1-75c3d2d72344","description":"A gang","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-791d-b9c3-3a4f6001fb4b","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which planet is known for having the Great Red Spot?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Jupiter\u2019s Great Red Spot is a giant storm in its atmosphere that has been observed for centuries.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7b8e-bad7-5500dfa42614","description":"Jupiter","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7608-b975-ab6bef4133ea","description":"Saturn","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7d65-8292-8f3b0a6a119f","description":"Mars","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7cb1-a291-4f72727d0a59","description":"Neptune","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7266-a3e3-2aedc81f809e","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Who discovered the structure of the atom?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Ernest Rutherford inferred the atom\'s compact, positively charged nucleus after some alpha particles bounced sharply off thin gold foil.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554e-746b-aa5d-8a25bc1f3584","description":"Ernest Rutherford","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7025-b9c2-781751e6d32d","description":"Albert Einstein","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-754a-9c7a-93321eef469b","description":"J. J. Thomson","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7179-872e-4d075840c391","description":"Niels Bohr","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7f1f-b80f-1f8258810af7","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the name for a hot spring that shoots 