","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-72e1-b4c1-75d128cad85f","description":"Bright","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7f64-8257-a1c87d46c1f6","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the tallest tree species in the world?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Coast redwoods can grow taller than 100 meters. Giant sequoias are generally shorter, though they are much bulkier.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7f94-90e5-fcd13929ddc3","description":"Coast Redwood","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-794a-b932-a251d010e67e","description":"Mountain Ash","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7465-8061-65c25d9c21dc","description":"Oak Tree","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7b0e-b73d-e1206da0810b","description":"Douglas Fir","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-764d-b8d5-b02032474138","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which fish is able to breathe air?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Lungfish have air-breathing organs, and some can survive drought buried in mud inside a mucus cocoon.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554e-71e9-aa15-a0fc660a704f","description":"Lungfish","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7607-91c2-3ec00a8f2f88","description":"Shark","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7df0-bdad-67a2067928cb","description":"Airfish","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7125-8faa-5327b7bf54bb","description":"Bubblefish","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7f26-90e3-e2eeee4d3f2d","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What are, on average, the heaviest primates?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Gorillas are the largest living primates. The name silverback refers to the pale hair that develops across a mature male\u2019s back.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554e-72f1-88a4-dad2f32fcec5","description":"Gorillas","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-704c-8c0c-a8484f6d7c28","description":"Humans","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7631-af1a-5c9c256b7236","description":"Orangutans","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7a36-923d-662745721576","description":"Chimpanzees","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-79a6-8a68-b62d7fcebd53","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which is NOT a source of renewable energy?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Petroleum forms over geological timescales from buried organic matter, so it is finite. Biomass, sunlight, and tidal motion are replenished naturally.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7483-81f9-e1ba9d2d8183","description":"Petroleum","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7242-bef5-75cea4df676d","description":"Biomass","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-72db-a413-59d2942eef74","description":"Sun","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-70e2-8bb5-8a066a9e7220","description":"Tides","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7739-9069-31f0359e9851","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"If you were travelling at mach 2 how fast would you be travelling?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Mach number compares an object\'s velocity with the local speed of sound, so Mach 2 is double that reference velocity.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7029-a187-31c2e3e067bc","description":"Twice the speed of sound","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7a74-ab92-fc9df4952472","description":"Twice the speed of light","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-721c-ae97-305a1129f757","description":"200 miles per hour","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7e48-8d63-b85c9d930fd4","description":"2 miles per second","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7891-9729-fa5d83beb8cd","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which of these scientific theories was an improvement over the theory of mechanics by Isaac Newton?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"General relativity extends Newtonian gravity and predicts that massive objects bend light, an effect confirmed by observations near the Sun.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7f5c-83bc-adecc65418d1","description":"General relativity","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7d3e-9d41-c0783d347c1b","description":"Lamarckism","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7b44-9c0f-6107a991329e","description":"Maxwell\'s equations","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7639-9ec2-f64dc3b53b1e","description":"Snell\'s law","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-731c-af82-19aecc000c27","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"How many neck vertebrae does a giraffe have?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Seven is also the usual number of neck vertebrae in humans; giraffes\u2019 vertebrae are simply much longer.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554e-79df-bcf1-bd3b6ad5bd69","description":"Seven","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-731f-bdd7-ace1ee90ee83","description":"Fourteen","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7b74-969f-e32b0ce66c2a","description":"Nine","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-72fa-ad48-e55e1e0f264b","description":"Twelve","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-719a-9902-b0e1d2755810","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the word used when one tectonic plate moves under another?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Subduction can create deep ocean trenches and volcanic arcs, and it is associated with powerful earthquakes.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7991-8a76-05c284db98c3","description":"Subduction","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7e0e-b47b-808d0593dcc3","description":"Profession","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-79f1-9bfa-c5bdbc863d4a","description":"Induction","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7a48-a387-14e68d8f68db","description":"Transgression","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7e15-ab6d-78104520f4a4","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Where in the body is the smallest human muscle?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The stapedius, the body\'s smallest skeletal muscle, is in the middle ear and helps limit the stapes\' movement in response to loud sounds.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7b22-a769-1d539f2dc885","description":"Ear","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7467-ac49-a3f7fb04449d","description":"Nose","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7c42-b658-4c0fb08898b3","description":"Hand","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7796-9a2d-610c8be5ebcb","description":"Foot","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7d39-8d51-d2330d7333b4","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the specialty of an ophthalmologist?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Ophthalmologists are medical doctors who can perform surgery to treat conditions affecting the eyes.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554e-750c-b355-ee00f0c6b184","description":"Eyes","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7b3a-ad48-b4ae94cf680d","description":"Testes","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7764-97f1-4126e92e33cc","description":"Kidneys","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7be6-bcf8-6588fdafcd5a","description":"Feet","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-770d-a421-11ede2035785","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"How many sides does a heptagon have?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The prefix hepta- comes from Greek for seven and also appears in heptathlon, an event with seven disciplines.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554e-779f-8f8f-86b6e48c3540","description":"7","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7b2d-a1bf-1b57e9a4dbbd","description":"8","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-705f-91c6-3ccc59d665fe","description":"6","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-70c5-910a-9780c52032cc","description":"9","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-72cc-b8b2-786833f304a9","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Hierology the study of?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Hierology broadly concerns sacred matters, while theology focuses more specifically on God and religious doctrine.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554e-790a-8fb5-aa5312bcce70","description":"a more inclusive term for theology","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7c89-9581-31eee249f134","description":"the history, languages, and cultures of the Indian subcontinent","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7f80-8d6d-5c099d8fc849","description":"the Sumerians","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7449-9c91-3e246ecef07d","description":"crayfish","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7763-9f01-76e2ff4b2d2b","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which gas, produced by bacteria, forms the holes in Swiss cheese?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"In Swiss cheese, propionic acid bacteria release carbon dioxide as they ferment, and the trapped bubbles form the characteristic holes.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7bdb-afed-5d5c10a2f260","description":"Carbon dioxide","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7886-8cd3-1aeeb5604624","description":"Oxygen","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-76fb-991b-522654905993","description":"Nitrogen","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7a2f-b443-be1b63785b6d","description":"Methane","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-79a5-b5ec-65b97106d997","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the name of a triangle with two sides of equal length?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"An isosceles triangle has at least two sides of equal length; when all three sides match, it is also equilateral.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb