culty":2,"explanation":"Elephants usually give birth to a single calf, which can stand and walk soon after birth.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554e-75ff-8dfc-714ecb5f5269","description":"Elephant","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7548-9e6c-4e83e95c15b0","description":"Tiger","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7b47-ade8-96e58b10c6d4","description":"Hippopotamus","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7e52-b81e-f8b106c392dd","description":"Giraffe","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-774d-9e72-e72f17085826","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the chemical sodium chloride often used for?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Sodium chloride is table salt; concentrated salt draws water out of microbes, helping slow spoilage.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554e-707b-a385-05965c589c0c","description":"It is commonly used as a condiment and food preservative.","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7560-84fa-f7a757e1a117","description":"It is used to relieve pain.","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7165-8245-1b0e61b4472d","description":"It is used in thermometers, thermostats, barometers","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7539-aa0b-7aa341798e7d","description":"It is used in nuclear reactors, as a neutron moderator.","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7235-b6da-23650294e395","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which plant has bright yellow blossoms that turn into round, fluffy seed heads?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Each dandelion seed has a fine, parachute-like tuft that helps the wind carry it away.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554e-79c6-81f7-91901efe3401","description":"Dandelion","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7a0f-bd50-993ce84d3efb","description":"Lily","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7f6f-99fc-578023c51403","description":"Aster","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-75ef-b1aa-938ff3552843","description":"Common flax","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-77e8-b620-0f126db9d4c4","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"With which animals is the disease myxomatosis associated?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Myxomatosis is caused by the myxoma virus. Australia used it in the 1950s to reduce rabbit populations, though resistance later increased.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7113-b90d-58da683d1554","description":"Rabbits","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7347-bfc1-7108bae485e5","description":"Chickens","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7269-b1ef-70e4821d7a87","description":"Pigs","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7ac8-a649-064d240fd337","description":"Sheep","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-71f6-a78d-a203d58552bd","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"As what is Polaris also known?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Polaris is called the North Star because it lies close to the north celestial pole and appears nearly fixed as other stars circle it.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554e-78cc-82ad-ece5343d5a63","description":"The North Star","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7fbd-84dc-f9664aefba2b","description":"Orion\'s Belt","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-79a4-97e7-172272e259ef","description":"The Sun","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7f2d-be05-24bcd7e4767e","description":"Alpha Centauri","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-74b7-8352-42fc6f9ceda3","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Audiology the study of?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Audiology also includes assessing hearing loss and fitting hearing aids.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7626-bf5d-4001099a423f","description":"Hearing","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-75d3-be5b-bd1275afef1e","description":"Bees","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-73d9-bcca-8e073e4f25ab","description":"The spread of diseases","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7b3f-9da6-76c5eee5697a","description":"Rocks","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7255-b2ad-573909149678","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the bending of light when it enters a different medium?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Refraction happens because light changes speed as it passes between materials, such as air and water, changing its direction.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554e-784d-b932-af8e6b5ea838","description":"Refraction","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7abc-bd45-ea6048615808","description":"Reflection","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-73f6-8899-4dfc93a0c724","description":"Convection","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7b79-ae08-8a2c92d4c6f2","description":"Ablation","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-77dc-b6ea-df63ddc4512b","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which substance takes its name from the Greek for `not flammable\'?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Asbestos fibers were used in insulation and other heat-resistant materials, but inhaling them can cause serious disease.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7dc0-adb1-43c07c0ad4f3","description":"Asbestos","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7b82-a3b7-599d75e8f88a","description":"Bleach","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7be7-9292-c7624fc8b454","description":"Ethanol","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-71a6-a88b-2f64010af453","description":"Methadone","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7e2e-9a3b-a9360907c028","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"In mammals, which organ produces milk?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Mammary glands are modified sweat glands, and prolactin helps stimulate milk production after birth.","alternatives