"difficulty":2,"explanation":"Roosters are known for their loud crowing call, which often signals the start of the day.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554e-73f3-8955-bc20e28c5f03","description":"A Rooster","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7b98-bdb7-f93a34c90d92","description":"A Buck","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7ab5-8178-a9416c3619cb","description":"A Dog","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7eda-9126-8be818951c1f","description":"A Ram","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7804-a5e6-88302e183a12","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What procedure involved cutting the connections to and from the prefrontal cortex of the brain?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Lobotomy\u2019s developer, Ant\u00f3nio Egas Moniz, received the 1949 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine for work on the therapeutic value of leucotomy.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7ec8-9733-ea63b5b24541","description":"Lobotomy","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-773b-be5a-ee06685ddad0","description":"Electroconvulsive therapy","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7da3-b213-20f23b8fd9d5","description":"Insulin shock therapy","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7c9b-b72b-0457ea836ca5","description":"Trepanning","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7328-b422-903f24a0469e","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the name of the physical law that states that energy is neither created or destroyed?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Law of Conservation of Energy says energy can change forms but the total remains constant in an isolated system.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7db3-b728-33ce516038d5","description":"Law of Conservation of Energy","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-7388-ae76-066844d14a03","description":"Law of Universal Gravitation","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218eb-554e-75b9-a095-5f978dcfa98b","des